(i) Senior HR Officer (all other 42H coded positions with no common title).', '25dc4cde45da1abb5e13da1d8181c037a04457fe3a603cca7347f01ce6f79a9a', 11, 12, '11', 145, null, null, false, null),
  ('3fc76819-bcea-5836-8684-a155056d4c42', 'd6d861cb-e0f0-5072-a443-90b256a47eb7', 'Army', 'officer', '42H', 'SENIOR HUMAN RESOURCES OFFICER', 'self_development', 'O-6', null, 'Colonel development — Self-development', 'Adjutant General Branch officer career pamphlet, DA PAM 600-3 chapter (26 January 2026)', 'Colonels should perfect leadership, managerial, and executive talents, apply those skills as creative and strategic thinkers, and display disciplines of governance, diplomacy, and statesmanship.', 'd0db366b9249fb3891a9a73d74ae1deec36c64259a08f2237a60106ba4c92538', 12, 12, '12', 146, null, null, false, null),
  ('c166620b-309d-5b5f-bb0a-653d3bd0f32a', 'd6d861cb-e0f0-5072-a443-90b256a47eb7', 'Army', 'officer', '42H', 'SENIOR HUMAN RESOURCES OFFICER', 'development', 'O-6', null, 'Colonel development — Desired experience', 'Adjutant General Branch officer career pamphlet, DA PAM 600-3 chapter (26 January 2026)', 'Colonels should be versatile and experienced strategic leaders and creative thinkers. The sum of their skills, assignments, experience, and development should have prepared them for key and influential positions. They should be the senior HR officer that mentors and ensures relevant and reliable HR support. Only a limited number of Adjutant General Officers are selected for CSL. Those officers not selected for CSL will continue to provide exceptional service in assignments within the Army. These officers also provide the critical bridge between the operating and generating force and serve as the advocate of commanders in staff positions at all echelons.', 'a697774d6c6b7f4600d9e22443dc8439b047452103fa02e562367dedfb1b30c1', 12, 12, '12', 147, null, null, false, null),
  ('5f986023-03db-56b1-9ba4-0a92aa6ee5fc', 'd6d861cb-e0f0-5072-a443-90b256a47eb7', 'Army', 'officer', '42H', 'SENIOR HUMAN RESOURCES OFFICER', 'development', 'O-6', null, 'Colonel development — Commanders of the USMA Band are selected by the USMA Superintendent', 'Adjutant General Branch officer career pamphlet, DA PAM 600-3 chapter (26 January 2026)', 'A panel that includes a USMA designated representative, the AG School Commandant, and the ASOM Commandant will provide an order of merit list to the Superintendent for selection. The selection process includes the applicant’s Soldier Talent Profile and a personal interview.', 'cfa4c9172a8feeb4ea0dc966aa20a7781445503dee85bb480074e26bf25b71ef', 12, 12, '12', 148, null, null, false, null),
  ('ae5a8f0e-4d67-515e-a3ca-2ac1e49ded0d', 'd6d861cb-e0f0-5072-a443-90b256a47eb7', 'Army', 'officer', '42H', 'SENIOR HUMAN RESOURCES OFFICER', 'development', 'O-6', null, 'Colonel development — Command tours are 36 months', 'Adjutant General Branch officer career pamphlet, DA PAM 600-3 chapter (26 January 2026)', 'USMA Commands may request one 12-month extension to the AG School Commandant (Proponent) with approval by an AG General Officer.', '28f077a631228597dc2a1e285b7260e80ee8ab6ff2de248c7a38934aaa04db60', 12, 12, '12', 149, null, null, false, null);
